    "titleMy": "多文化共生社会におけるコミュニケーションのあり方 (Communication in a Multicultural Coexistence Society) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "多文化共生社会におけるコミュニケーションのあり方 (Communication in a Multicultural Coexistence Society) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "With the increase of foreign residents living in Japan, promoting \"multicultural coexistence\" in local communities has become a vital task. In a society where people of differing nationalities and native languages live together, respecting each other's positions and ways of thinking is indispensable.\n\nFor individuals whose native tongue is not Japanese, comprehending the complex kanji and technical terminology lined up in official city hall documents and disaster prevention pamphlets is exceptionally difficult. Confronting language barriers during everyday life procedures becomes a major cause of isolation and anxiety for them.\n\nToward such challenges, local municipalities nationwide are proactively promoting information provision using \"Plain Japanese\" (Yasashii Nihongo). This holds the significant merit of being easy to understand not only for foreigners, but also for elderly individuals and children. The stance of every resident placing themselves in the other person's perspective and facing them with a kind attitude leads directly to creating communities where everyone can live with peace of mind."
