    "translationMy": "Accompanying modern city development, reconstruction of dilapidated buildings and redevelopment projects are proceeding nationwide. However, despite colossal taxes and expenses having been invested, commercial facilities that fail to satisfactorily meet residents' expectations are also observed. Voices of criticism such as \"people don't gather\" and \"the community's unique charm was lost\" are not uncommon.\n\nOn the other hand, in a shopping street in a certain provincial city, without venturing into large-scale redevelopment, an initiative was conducted to preserve old streetscapes while leasing vacant stores to young creators. Considering its limited budget, this venture yielded great outcomes and is gathering attention from across the nation. Considering the exteriors of the buildings are old, inside they are lined with clean, sophisticated cafes and ateliers, bustling with youths and tourists.\n\nSpending vast expenses does not guarantee success. Accurately projecting the region's current circumstances and residents' needs, and providing genuinely desired value, is precisely the key to sustainable town planning."
