    "titleMy": "現代社会における「プチ不調」のサインを見逃さない (Catching Subtle Signals of Poor Health in Modern Society) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "現代社会における「プチ不調」のサインを見逃さない (Catching Subtle Signals of Poor Health in Modern Society) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "“It is not a full-blown illness, but my body feels somewhat sluggish”; “When waking up in the morning, my head feels heavy and I feel slightly sleep-deprived.” People harboring such subtle minor ailments are increasing among modern businesspersons and students. Even though tests reveal no abnormalities, it is a delicate hint that mind and body cannot be deemed in perfect condition.\n\nEspecially during periods when pressure mounts such as before project deadlines or examinations, people tend to finish meals simply without realizing it and are apt to slip into lack of exercise. Even when feeling tired, they tend to pile on unreasonable burdens thinking “this much is okay,” ignoring the signals from their own bodies.\n\nHowever, whether one takes appropriate rest at early stages such as a touch of a cold or slight fatigue significantly determines subsequent health. If you feel condition is even slightly dipping, adjustments such as avoiding staying up late, soaking in a warm bath, and securing ample sleep are necessary. Thoroughly understanding the tendencies of your own mind and body on a daily basis and not overlooking small ailments forms the bedrock of a fulfilling daily life."
