    "titleMy": "Crisis Management in Municipal Railway Operations (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "Crisis Management in Municipal Railway Operations (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "In modern urban transit systems, second-by-second accuracy and rapid communication are indispensable conditions for protecting passenger safety. Especially during abnormal weather such as heavy snow or typhoons, conditions change minute by minute, and on-site response speed can even determine life or death.\n\nOne evening, torrential rain created the risk of an embankment slope collapsing beside the tracks. The moment the safety monitoring sensor detected precipitation exceeding the danger threshold, alarms blared across the central operations center. Dispatchers immediately issued an emergency stop directive to all trains.\n\nImmediately after the trains safely stopped, station and onboard announcements began guiding passengers. The railway operations manual specifies: \"As soon as safety at the site is verified, slow-speed service will resume.\" However, in natural disasters, one must never hastily rush service resumption. Ensuring safety is paramount; upon verifying safety, staff are required to promptly share information and proceed with utmost caution."
