    "translationMy": "This summer, because of localized torrential rains striking western Japan, our town's prideful organic vegetable farm suffered severe muddy flood damage. Most of the tomato and eggplant fields just before harvest were buried in mud, leaving farmers who had poured devotion into their crops for years in deep despair. Because of nature's fury in the sudden weather shift, a year's worth of efforts was on the verge of being wasted in an instant.\n\nHowever, what saved this dire predicament was warm goodwill from across the country. Thanks to volunteers who learned of the situation via social media rushing over every weekend, mud clearance operations progressed at a pace beyond expectations. Furthermore, thanks to materials supplied by neighboring municipalities and technical guidance from agricultural cooperatives, soil disinfection and replanting of seedlings were completed early.\n\nThanks to the support of people who rushed to assist, we were safely able to harvest a portion of our vegetables in autumn. Although we suffered a heavy blow because of a natural disaster, reconfirming the warmth of human ties became an irreplaceable, precious asset for the town."
  },
