    "translationMy": "Takahashi-san, who was spending busy days at an IT company in a metropolitan city, was exhausted both physically and mentally from packed commuter trains every morning and overtime lasting late into the night. Although his monthly salary was high, on weekdays he barely secured enough sleep, and weekends were spent merely sleeping to recover from fatigue.\n\nOne day, while receiving an IV drip after his health collapsed, Takahashi-san reexamined his way of living. He felt intensely convinced: \"Rather than enduring work for the sake of high income to the point of ruining my mental and physical health, wouldn't shifting to an environment where I can value my own time, even with a reduced income, be far richer?\"\n\nSeveral months later, Takahashi-san boldly resigned from the company and relocated to a mountainous town in Nagano Prefecture surrounded by rich nature. His new life renovating an old traditional house, growing vegetables self-sufficiently, and doing light remote tasks lacks metropolitan convenience, but is embraced by the clear morning air and tranquility.\n\nTakahashi-san reflects: \"Nothing in life is as irreplaceable a luxury as feeling the shift of the four seasons on one's skin and sharing peaceful time with family and local community members.\" He finally realized that peace of mind each day is true wealth surpassing any financial success he had previously chased."
  },
