    "translationMy": "In modern society, corporate activities must not merely pursue profit, but prioritize fairness and ethics. Legal compliance is the bare minimum duty for corporate survival; companies should never engage in illegal conduct regardless of the reason. If defective products cause social harm, management cannot avoid promptly disclosing facts and offering a heartfelt apology. Furthermore, companies should uphold higher social norms such as environmental protection and consideration for diverse talents, fulfilling moral obligations for future generations."
