    "titleMyanmar": "Disaster Prevention Science: Analyzing River Flood Data to Prevent Urban Inundation (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "Due to abnormal weather from recent global warming, record-breaking downpours have occurred frequently across Japan. Especially in river basins and urban centers, torrential rain exceeding drainage capacities heightens flooding risks. Data analysis of past flood disasters reveals that evacuation delay is a primary factor aggravating damage. Unlike earthquakes, floods can be predicted in advance through radar and water level data. However, from the fact that people fall into normalcy bias thinking \"it has never flooded before so it is fine,\" many residents fail to act when evacuation orders are issued. Preparing hazard maps and confirming evacuation routes during normal times is fundamental to saving lives."
