    "titleMyanmar": "都市防災と最新テクノロジーの活用 (Urban Disaster Prevention & Technology Application) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "Due to its geographical conditions, Japan is a nation where natural disasters such as earthquakes, typhoons, and localized torrential downpours frequently break out. In the past, through communication delays and infrastructure vulnerability, enormous human and material damages were often brought about.\n\nHowever today, due to the remarkable development of information technology (IT), the approach toward disaster countermeasures has transformed dramatically. For instance, through high-precision meteorological satellite data and AI analysis, the forecast accuracy of typhoon paths and rainfall has surged remarkably. Thereby, early issuance of evacuation advisories became feasible, achieving substantial reductions in casualties caused by floods.\n\nFurthermore, through the emergency earthquake early warning distribution system via smartphones, people have become able to take action seconds to tens of seconds before strong tremors arrive and secure their bodily safety. In addition, rapid rescue operations utilizing cutting-edge tech, such as situational verification of affected disaster zones by drones, are progressing.\n\nWhile preventing natural disasters entirely is difficult, through human wisdom and technological progress, society is steadily advancing the realization of \"disaster mitigation\"—keeping damages caused by disasters to an absolute minimum."
