    "translationMy": "Matsumoto: Kawaguchi-kun, good work today. During the meeting earlier, your voice was somewhat raspy and you looked like you had a touch of a cold; are you all right?\nKawaguchi: Matsumoto-senpai, thank you very much for noticing. Actually my throat has been hurting since last night, and I feel a touch feverish.\nMatsumoto: As I suspected. Lately overtime has continued constantly, and you were apt to become sleep-deprived. Shall I take over preparing the presentation materials for this evening on your behalf?\nKawaguchi: No, it troubles my conscience to ask you, senpai. If I push myself, I think I can somehow finish it.\nMatsumoto: Pushing yourself when in poor health is the worst thing to do. Rather than worsening the cold and being absent from work for days, you should leave early today and visit a clinic.\nKawaguchi: Thank you very much for your care. Then I will accept your kind offer, leave today's work to you, senpai, and rest early."
