      "id": "n3.l23.g001",
      "lessonId": "n3.l23",
      "pattern": "〜というわけではない / 〜わけではない",
      "meaning": "it does not necessarily mean that ... / not always the case that ...",
      "formation": "[Verb / い-Adj Plain] + わけではない\n[な-Adj な] + わけではない\n[Noun （という）] + わけではない",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "Used for partial negation, denying an absolute generalization or an assumption that the listener might logically infer. It clarifies that while a certain condition exists, the extreme conclusion does not automatically follow.",
        "my": "အရာအားလုံးကို အလုံးစုံငြင်းပယ်ခြင်းမဟုတ်ဘဲ \"ထိုသို့ဖြစ်သည်နှင့် ထိုသို့လုံးဝဖြစ်ရမည်ဟု မဆိုလိုပါ\" ဟု အစိတ်အပိုင်းတစ်ခုကိုသာ ယဉ်ကျေးစွာ ခြွင်းချက်ပြုငြင်းဆိုရာတွင် သုံးသည်။"
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "sentenceId": "n3.l23.s006",
          "note": "Expensive products are not necessarily superior in quality"
        },
        {
          "sentenceId": "n3.l23.s009",
          "note": "Not hating the job, but seeking higher challenges"
        }
      ],
      "similarGrammarIds": [],
      "commonMistakes": [
        "Do not confuse with 〜わけがない (which is an emphatic 100% denial of possibility: \"there is no way...\"). 〜わけではない is gentle partial negation (\"not necessarily...\")."
      ],
      "level": "N3",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "prov": {
        "source": "Nihongo N2 Master Editorial Team (AI-Assisted Editorial Authoring)",
        "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
