    "translationMy": "Ten years have passed since I left my hometown to live in the city. With changes in work and environment, old memories feel like they fade, but every time I return home once a year and step onto the station platform, nostalgic air and memories vividly revive. The old shopping district has gradually transformed ever since large shopping complexes spread, and bustling mom-and-pop shops have dwindled. Seeing these changes in cityscape and urban structure, I am struck by how fast times change. Yet, reuniting with childhood friends and teachers reassures me that the warmth of people has remained unchanged."
